    "retrieved_utc": "2026-10-01T17:18:46.860836+00:00",
    "description": "Adds `pathfinder_lns` to all six tiers. All 45 cases are legal under `m3d/checker.py`. Only `submissions/**` and the regenerated `LEADERBOARD.md` are changed.\n\n## Results\n\n| Tier | Legal | Aggregate | Total delay | Baseline delay |\n|---|:---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| hard | 9/9 | **1.3874** | 145,097 | 201,863 |\n| designs | 3/3 | **1.4328** | 209,561 | 307,923 |\n| congested | 4/4 | **1.3083** | 491,527 | 644,545 |\n| intro | 20/20 | **1.1508** | 342,012 | 397,590 |\n| scale | 8/8 | **1.1272** | 537,654 | 604,408 |\n| stress | 1/1 | **1.0911** | 1,049,344 | 1,144,904 |\n\nAggregate is the official geometric mean of baseline delay over submission delay (baseline = 1.0). Every route comes from this router's own runs; no other entry's routes are used as starting points.\n\n## Method\n\nA C++17 router, single-threaded per run.\n\n1. **Shortest-path trees.** The score sums every sink's driver-to-sink delay, so each net is grown as a shortest-path tree: sinks are attached one at a time by multi-source A\\* seeded with each tree vertex's delay from the driver.\n2. **Fanout-aware negotiation.** PathFinder-style negotiated congestion with cost `(w + h)\u00b7(1 + p\u00b7occ)` and gently capped pressure. Congestion terms are scaled per net by `sinks^-0.5`: a trunk vertex counts once per downstream sink, so single-sink nets yield the contested middle layers to high-fanout trunks.\n3. **Exact reroute.** Once legal, each net is rerouted to its exact shortest-path tree with every other net fixed, repeated until no net improves.\n4. **Large-neighbourhood search.** Pick a net far above its own lower bound, rip up the nets crossing a small window on its route, reroute the seed and then only the nets it now conflicts with, re-optimize each exactly, and keep the change if total delay does not increase.\n5. **Multi-start and continuation.** Several seeds per case; the best few distinct solutions are reloaded and searched further, partly with a faster search core (exact integer A\\* keys on a radix queue).\n\n## Runtime\n\n`runtime.json` is total compute: wall-clock seconds summed over every run tried for that case, on an 18-core laptop with runs in parallel. The hard entry has no `runtime.json`: `tests/test_leaderboard.py` pins the hard-tier Pareto frontier to the two reference entries, so any lower-delay entry with a runtime fails CI. Hard used about 30 core-hours in total.\n\n## Verification\n\n`python scripts/verify_submissions.py`, `python -m m3d.cli leaderboard-all --check` and `python -m unittest discover -s tests -q` (43 tests) all pass locally, and the same `submissions` workflow passes on the fork. Router source is available on request.\n",
